To convert the response body into a custom Dart object, you can use the `dart:convert` package to decode the response body into a JSON Map, and then use a factory method like `fromJson()` to parse it [6]. For example:

```dart
class Album {
  final int userId;
  final int id;
  final String title;

  const Album({required this.userId, required this.id, required this.title});

  factory Album.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
    return switch (json) {
      {'userId': int userId, 'id': int id, 'title': String title} => Album(
        userId: userId,
        id: id,
        title: title,
      ),
      _ => throw const FormatException('Failed to load album.'),
    };
  }
}
```

You can then call this inside your network request function when the server returns a 200 OK response [6]:

```dart
return Album.fromJson(jsonDecode(response.body) as Map<String, dynamic>);
```
